   "subject": "cutw function resulting in output that is one sample too long when starting at t > 0",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">It looks like this issue occurs only when cutw is called with from &gt; 0 <div><br></div><div>such that<div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"> cutw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tico</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">from</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> to </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> output </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Wave&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br> gives you an output that is 1 tico-sample-rate (22050 samples) long.<br><br>However, if instead you run <div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">cutw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tico</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">from</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> to </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> output </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Wave&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br>, you get one extra sample (output is length 22051).</div><div><br></div><div>I believe that the error is found in the line <div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">else</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> a </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> round</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">from</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> f</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></div></code></div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br> </span></div><div><br></div><div>Which should be <div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">else</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> a </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> round</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">from</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> f</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span></div></code></div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
