     "<div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:#000000\"><div>Thank you very much David for noting this. I will apply the correction in the next release.</div><div>Best</div><div>Jerome</div><div><div><div style=\"color:#000000;font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><br></div></div></div><hr><div><b>De: </b>&quot;David Savage&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">davidt...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br><b>À: </b>&quot;seewave GROUP&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">see...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br><b>Envoyé: </b>Jeudi 14 Mai 2020 04:59:26<br><b>Objet: </b>[seewave] cutw function resulting in output that is one sample too long when starting at t &gt; 0<br></div><div><br></div><div></div></div></div>"
